      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Rail service began on May 23, 1853, after a railroad was built through the area, marking Kappa’s early connection to the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kappa%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kappa sits on the north side of the Mackinaw River, just five miles from both Lake Bloomington and Evergreen Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
